---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '~/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '~/config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms for reading Mindful: a free demo and portfolio project, offered as is, with no warranty and no professional advice."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[52rem]">
    <PageHeader title="Using Mindful on fair terms." crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]} />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        By reading Mindful you agree to these terms. If they do not work for you, please stop using
        the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What Mindful is</h2>
      <p>
        Mindful is a demo and portfolio project: a small, free website of short essays on everyday
        mental wellbeing. It is reading material, not therapy, coaching or crisis support. Nothing
        here replaces advice from a qualified professional. The <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>
        explains the limits of the content and where to find help in a crisis.
      </p>

      <h2>As is, with no warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The essays and the site are provided as is. We make no promise that the content is complete,
        accurate or up to date, or that the site will always be available or free of errors. We may
        change or remove essays, pages and these terms at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent the law allows, Mindful and its editors are not liable for any loss or
        damage arising from your use of the site or from relying on any essay.
      </p>

      <h2>Who owns what</h2>
      <p>
        The site&rsquo;s code is public on <a href={siteConfig.repoUrl}>GitHub</a> under the MIT
        licence, so you can reuse it as long as you keep the copyright notice. The essays still
        belong to the project owners. You are welcome to link to any page, but please ask before
        copying an essay elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party material belongs to its owners. That includes the placeholder photos from
        Picsum, the Fraunces and Newsreader typefaces, and any site an essay links to. We do not
        control linked sites and are not responsible for them.
      </p>

      <h2>Fair use of the site</h2>
      <p>
        Do not try to break, overload or probe the site in ways that could harm other readers, and
        do not use it to harass anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy and questions</h2>
      <p>
        What happens to technical data when you visit is described on the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> page. For questions about these terms, open an issue on
        <a href={siteConfig.issuesUrl}>the Mindful repository on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
